An HTTP service on the lacodda line's stack: Rust, [axum](https://github.com/tokio-rs/axum),
sqlx and Postgres. Scaffolded with [lyrn](https://github.com/lacodda/lyrn).

## A day in the life

```console
$ docker compose -f deploy/compose.yml up -d db    # a database to talk to
$ export DATABASE_URL=postgres://{{ lib_name }}:...@localhost:5432/{{ lib_name }}
$ cargo run                                        # migrations run at startup
$ curl localhost:8080/api/health
{"status":"ok","version":"0.1.0"}
```

```console
$ cargo fmt --check && cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings && cargo test
```

That is the gate CI runs. The tests skip themselves when `DATABASE_URL` is
unset, which is right on a laptop without a database - CI always provides one,
so the suite is never green and blind.

## Configuration

Everything comes from the environment, so the same binary runs in a container,
on a stand and on a laptop without a config file to keep in step:

| Variable | Default | What it does |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `DATABASE_URL` | *required* | Postgres connection string |
| `{{ env_prefix }}_BIND` | `0.0.0.0:8080` | Where to listen |
| `{{ env_prefix }}_POOL_SIZE` | `5` | Database connections to keep |
| `RUST_LOG` | — | `info`, `debug`, or a per-module filter |

## Deploying

```console
$ cp deploy/env.example deploy/.env    # then edit it
$ docker compose -f deploy/compose.yml up -d --build
```

The image is built on the target machine, which makes every deploy a proof
that the code builds for that architecture.

## Migrations

`migrations/` holds plain SQL, applied at startup: a binary and the schema it
expects travel together, so there is no window where one is ahead of the other.
Add a file with a later prefix; never edit one that has run somewhere.

## Layout

| Path | What lives there |
| --- | --- |
| `src/app.rs` | Every route the service answers, in one place |
| `src/config.rs` | What it needs to know, and where it reads it from |
| `src/error.rs` | One error type, mapped to status codes once |
| `migrations/` | The schema, as plain SQL |
| `deploy/` | Compose file for a stand |
| `docs/adr/` | Architecture decisions, newest last |

